 2. 🏈 Flightmare jumbles college kickoffs 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Covers of today's New York Post and California Post. 

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The nationwide ground stop left NBA, NHL and college teams scrambling to reach their destinations in time for this weekend's games.

 No. 19 Mississippi's football game at Oklahoma was moved from today to Sunday, usually reserved for the NFL, at 1 p.m. EST. The SEC said the Ole Miss football team couldn't leave Oxford last night and will travel this afternoon. Oklahoma athletic director Roger Denny ripped the decision, saying the SEC threatened Oklahoma with a forfeit if it didn't agree to the move. Go deeper . ⏱️ Lots of today's kickoff times are changing. Most college football teams travel the day before their game, and several teams returned to campus from the airport, AP reports. 

 Auburn opted to take a bus to Mississippi State, with the SEC pushing back today's start time from noon EST to 4:15 p.m. to give the Tigers a little buffer. Purdue likewise decided to board buses from West Lafayette, Indiana, for its game at Iowa. NFL teams playing Sunday typically travel the day before their games. They were expected to fly as planned today.

