 3. 🤖 AI&#x27;s trust collapse 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump handed AI titans an extraordinary mandate six weeks ago: Police yourselves .

 But the industry faces a four-pronged crisis of trust as Democrats surge to power and many Americans rebel over AI and data centers , Axios' Erica Pandey reports. Guardrails for the industry will be a priority for the new Congress, with some populist Republicans eager to pile on. The big picture: Trump announced in late September that top AI CEOs had agreed to a voluntary safety accord . Since then, four crises have converged:

 🏛️ 1. The political crisis: AI was on the ballot for the first time during the midterm elections through a series of data center measures across America. People voted against data centers in 40 out of 41 cases, and swing-state incumbents linked to the facilities, including Sen. Jon Husted (R-Ohio) and Texas Gov. Greg Abbott (R), were voted out.

 Democrats are planning to unleash a flood of AI bills when they take control of Congress in January. They'll also bring some of the most powerful AI executives to D.C. to testify. 🦺 2. The safety crisis: OpenAI's Hugging Face breach , revealed in July , was a terrifying look at what could happen if machines operate beyond humans' control — and it was the first in a wave of revelations through the summer and fall.

 AI CEOs and engineers came forward with stark warnings about the dangers of the tech they've been building, including its potential to destroy humanity. 💰 3. The financial crisis: The AI trade is looking more vulnerable as investors question when or whether the industry's sky-high spending will deliver sky-high returns.

 Tech stocks tumbled , with Nvidia falling 13% this week amid the ouster of founder and CEO Jensen Huang. The stock has lost nearly 25% of its value since the first New York Times report in late October about Huang's links to a suspected Chinese spy. 🧐 4. The leadership crisis: Huang's stunning resignation is raising new questions about the vulnerability of the people running America's most powerful companies. 

 Pop culture has turned on the AI titans , with three year-end films — " The Social Reckoning " and " Musk ," out last month, and " Artificial ," opening Christmas Day — savaging Mark Zuckerberg, Elon Musk and OpenAI CEO Sam Altman. Get Axios AI+ , our daily tech newsletter. 

 
 
