 5. 🥕 Fresh inflation fears 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Americans are already paying more for groceries — and new inflation data this week suggests that the pressure is not letting up, Axios' Courtenay Brown reports. 

 The latest: Food prices are rising sharply even before they reach supermarket shelves. 📈 Wholesale fresh and dry vegetable prices surged 27% last month, adding to a 31% price jump the previous month. 

 These are the prices paid by food distributors, grocery chains and other businesses to farmers and other producers for eventual sale to consumers. Zoom in: Unusually warm weather, crop disease and insect infestations have reduced lettuce and other leafy green harvests in California.

 The Iran war has driven up the cost of fertilizer and fuel, making it more expensive to grow and transport food. 🥬 Case in point: A regional grocery chain recently told Fed officials that it now costs more to transport a head of lettuce from California than to buy the lettuce itself, citing high diesel fuel prices.

 Go deeper : High transportation costs drive wholesale prices. 
 
