 6. 🇨🇳 MAGA turns on Lutnick 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick steps off Marine One and walks into the White House last Sunday. Photo: Joey Sussman/ZUMA Press Commerce Secretary Lutnick has become the face of the Trump administration's troubled response to Chinese espionage and potential national security threats, Axios' Maria Curi and Marc Caputo report. 

 The most intense scrutiny is coming from Republicans on the Hill, fellow Cabinet members and the MAGA base. Why it matters: Regulators and policymakers on both sides of the aisle want someone's head for an affair that may have exposed sensitive technology to the nation's top foreign adversary.

 Two names are currently at the top of that list: former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang — and now Howard Lutnick. Get Axios 2028 , our weekly newsletter on the presidential race. 

 
 
