 7. 🌆 It&#x27;s &quot;Grand Theft Auto VI&quot; week 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A screenshot of Vice City from "Grand Theft Auto VI." Photo: Rockstar Games We're five days away from "Grand Theft Auto VI" going live, and the madness may be unlike anything we've seen before, Axios' Herb Scribner writes. 

 "GTA VI" has been in development for nearly 15 years and is shaping up to be the year's biggest cultural phenomenon. Millions of Americans are already planning on skipping work so they can drive around in slick cars and commit virtual crimes. The game, which cost Rockstar Games more than $2 billion to make, has already earned more than $1 billion from preorders.

 🚗 The new "Grand Theft Auto" finally arrives Thursday. Pre-loading of the 212 GB files began last week.

 The buzz  is off the charts. The game has already sold at least 11 million copies, per Sensor Tower . Launch gallery 

 
 
